From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reilly Brogan <reilly@reillybrogan.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] meson: drop the api-util test

The 3.0.8 release tarball is missing tests/api/test-util.c (it is present in
the git tree but was excluded from the generated dist tarball), which makes
`meson setup` fail with:

  meson.build:356:20: ERROR: File tests/api/test-util.c does not exist.

Remove the test definition until upstream ships a corrected tarball. This
patch should be dropped when updating to 3.0.9 (or any later release whose
dist tarball includes tests/api/test-util.c).

Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-09
---
 meson.build | 16 ----------------
 1 file changed, 16 deletions(-)

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -352,22 +352,6 @@
   build_by_default : false)
 test('api-serialize', test_api_serialize_exe)
 
-# Unit test for spdxtool's util uri encode.
-test_api_util_exe = executable('test-api-util',
-  'tests/api/test-util.c',
-  'cli/spdxtool/core.c',
-  'cli/spdxtool/software.c',
-  'cli/spdxtool/serialize.c',
-  'cli/spdxtool/simplelicensing.c',
-  'cli/spdxtool/util.c',
-  windows_manifest,
-  link_with : libpkgconf,
-  c_args : build_static,
-  include_directories : [include_directories('.'), include_directories('tests/api'), include_directories('cli/spdxtool')],
-  install : false,
-  build_by_default : false)
-test('api-util', test_api_util_exe)
-
 
 # Allocation-failure (OOM) tests.  These drive the shared fuzzer/alloc-inject
 # fault injector through the linker's --wrap, so they are built wherever --wrap
